# AVI ELF II / Hyperboard 32 KiB ROM — Netronics-compatible experiment.
# Approved architecture: docs/AVI_NETRONICS_ROM_APPROVED_DESIGN.md
# Reversible development only. Do not overwrite the proven 875B One ROM.
#
# CPU logical ROM address   Allocated     Component
# $8000-$97FF               6144 bytes    AVI / Elf2K monitor
# $9800-$A0FF               2304 bytes    AVI HELP
# $A100-$A3FF                768 bytes    reserved
# $A400-$B0FF               3328 bytes    EDTASM (XMODEM S/L disabled)
# $B100-$C1FF               4352 bytes    reserved
# $C200-$CFFF               3584 bytes    cassette service + padding
# $D000-$D7FF               2048 bytes    CHIP-8 loader + ROM spare
# $D800-$DCFF               1280 bytes    1979 CHIP-8 interpreter/OS/games
# $DD00-$EFFF               4864 bytes    reserved for future services
# $F000-$F0FF                256 bytes    ORIGINAL GIANT MONITOR, unchanged
# $F100-$F2FF                512 bytes    reserved
# $F300-$FFFF               3328 bytes    extended BIOS/BIOS
#
# CDP1861/PIXIE test enabled; original Weisbecker bitmap substituted
# in disposable AVI assembler input by avi-port.py.
# THIS TEST VARIANT DEFAULTS DIRECTLY TO COM2 38400 8N1; no COM1 EF4 jumper needed.
# COM1 Q/EF4 retained as an opt-in command only; restoring J15 required to use it.
# COM2 CDP1854 is optional: 9600 8N1 presently proven.
# COM2 19200 and 38400 owner hardware tested successfully (October 2026).
# External TCLK/RCLK must match selected x16 baud (307.2/614.4 kHz).
# Netronics Tiny BASIC executes separately from RAM starting at $0000.
#
# This configuration affects ONLY the AVI variant; stock Elf2K builds intact.
BOOTS=08000H
WARMB=($(strip $(BOOTS))+3)
RAMPAGE=07F00H

HELP=09800H
BIOS=0FF00H
EBIOS=0F800H
EDTASM=0A400H
GIANT=0F000H
PIXIE=1

# ROM CHIP8 commands copy the verified 1979 Netronics interpreter to RAM,
# retaining loaded game RAM 0200-09FF and enabling 1802 interrupts via 0E80.
# Experimental ROM build; four-squares and Maze command paths still await
# verification on hardware after their integration into this firmware.
